{"id": "63b8b46d-548d-4741-90a5-29bc6f19cbe6", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T17:37:17.374952", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-22T17:36\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "de04dfe7-15da-4861-b6c2-7b2133a294e7", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T17:37:17.377084", "source": "user", "parent_id": "63b8b46d-548d-4741-90a5-29bc6f19cbe6", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"请先只做检查工作，暂时不要给出完整方案或任何执行结果。我需要你完成三件事：\\n\\n一、输入与代码检查（只读，不运行实验）\\n1. 在 /workspace 仓库中定位 zero bubble 流水线并行相关的实现与仿真入口，列出具体文件与关键类/函数名称，并说明 1F1B、1F1B-I（即 1F1B-interleaved / 交错式）、ZB-1p、ZB-2p 这四种方法在代码中各自对应的调度构造路径。\\n2. 说明仓库中是否已存在吞吐量的计算或估计工具（例如仿真器、时间模型、cost model、bubble 比例计算、microbatch 数与 stage 数/层数的参数接口）。若存在，请给出接口名称与所需输入字段；若不存在，请明确指出缺失项。\\n3. 说明这四种方法在代码层面可配置的实际维度：microbatch 数量、pipeline stage（device）数量、模型层数/层划分方式、重计算（recompute）与交错（interleaved）开关、内存或显存约束参数。请只报告代码中真实存在的参数，不要推测。\\n4. 说明仓库自带的环境与依赖情况，以及是否存在官方示例脚本、单元测试或已有测试配置可作为实验设计依据。\\n\\n二、提出拟定方法（仅设计与理由，不做实现与跑数）\\n基于你检查到的实际代码结构，提出一份实验设计草案的骨架，至少包括：\\n- 被考察变量与响应变量（自变量：microbatch 数量；因变量：吞吐量，以及为解释吞吐量差异所需的 bubble 占比等辅助量）的定义与取值方式；\\n- 需要固定的控制变量（stage 数、层数与层划分、单 microbatch 的计算量假设、重计算策略等）及固定理由；\\n- 四种方法的比较安排，特别是\\\"ZB-2p 在 microbatch 较少时仍保持较高吞吐\\\"这一部分需要哪些额外的对照点（例如与 1F1B、ZB-1p 在相同小 microbatch 档位上的并列比较）；\\n- 分析计划（如何判断\\\"随 microbatch 增加而提升\\\"这一趋势，如何处理非单调情形）；\\n- 可行性评估（在无可运行计算资源的前提下，本设计如何以设计文档形式交付，以及若日后具备仿真条件所需的最低输入）。\\n\\n三、请明确列出你的假设与不确定之处\\n包括但不限于：microbatch 档位的选取依据、吞吐量口径（tokens/s、iter/s 或相对归一化时间）、是否允许以仿真时间代替真实计时、以及任何在仓库中查不到而必须作为假设对待的设定。凡属未在代码或文档中找到依据的选择，请标注为\\\"假设\\\"，不要表述为已确认的事实。请在回复中区分\\\"仓库中核实到的内容\\\"与\\\"你的建议\\\"，并附上你据以判断的文件路径或符号名称。\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the throughput for methods 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p improve as the number of microbatches increases, while ZB-2p maintains high throughput even with fewer microbatches? (Note: These methods are implemented as part of the zero bubble pipeline parallelism strategies in this repository, which aim to reduce pipeline bubbles and maintain high throughput.)\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
